    "gold_solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"VRPTW\")\n    m.setParam('TimeLimit', 300)\n\n    # --- Data ---\n    n_customers = 5\n    n_vehicles = 3\n    Q = 49  # vehicle capacity\n    vehicle_fixed_cost = 100.0\n    depot = [50, 50]\n    customers = [[41, 83], [20, 56], [48, 35], [86, 18], [33, 9]]\n    demands = [11, 22, 19, 23, 24]\n    time_windows = [[0, 293], [53, 123], [31, 131], [13, 106], [48, 99], [51, 125]]\n    service_times = [8, 14, 14, 13, 13]\n\n    # Node 0 = depot, nodes 1..N = customers\n    N = n_customers\n    nodes = list(range(N + 1))\n    cust_nodes = list(range(1, N + 1))\n\n    # Coordinates: index 0 = depot, 1..N = customers\n    coords = [depot] + customers\n\n    # COMPUTE distance matrix from coordinates\n    dist = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                dist[(i,j)] = math.sqrt(\n                    (coords[i][0]-coords[j][0])**2 +\n                    (coords[i][1]-coords[j][1])**2)\n\n    # Service time by node (depot = 0)\n    svc = [0] + service_times\n\n    # Big-M for time linking\n    T_max = time_windows[0][1]\n    max_svc = max(service_times)\n    max_dist = max(dist.values())\n    M = T_max + max_svc + max_dist + 1\n\n    # --- Variables ---\n    # Arc variables (binary)\n    x = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                x[(i,j)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Arc_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # Load variables (MTZ subtour elimination)\n    u = {}\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        u[i] = m.addVar(lb=demands[i-1], ub=Q, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Load_{i}\")\n\n    # Time variables\n    t = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        a, b = time_windows[i]\n        t[i] = m.addVar(lb=a, ub=b, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Time_{i}\")\n    # Fix depot departure to time 0\n    t[0].ub = 0.0\n\n    # --- Objective ---\n    # Minimize travel distance + vehicle fixed costs\n    obj = quicksum(dist[(i,j)] * x[(i,j)] for i in nodes for j in nodes if i != j)\n    obj += quicksum(vehicle_fixed_cost * x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes)\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # --- Constraints ---\n    # 1. Each customer has exactly one outgoing arc\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for j in nodes if j != i) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitOut_C{i}\")\n\n    # 2. Each customer has exactly one incoming arc\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for i in nodes if i != j) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitIn_C{j}\")\n\n    # 3. At most K vehicles leave the depot\n    m.addConstr(\n        quicksum(x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes) <= n_vehicles,\n        name=\"VehicleLimit\")\n\n    # 4. MTZ subtour elimination\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        for j in cust_nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    u[i] - u[j] + Q * x[(i,j)] <= Q - demands[j-1],\n                    name=f\"MTZ_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # 5. Time linking: if arc (i,j) is used, arrival at j >= departure from i\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        for i in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    t[i] - t[j] + M * x[(i,j)] <= M - svc[i] - dist[(i,j)],\n                    name=f\"TimeLink_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Subject: Routing and Scheduling Plan for Today\u2019s Multi-Stop Deliveries\n\nContext\nOur delivery operation dispatches a fleet of identical vehicles from a single central depot to serve a set of customer locations within the planning horizon. All vehicles begin their routes at time 0 and must be back at the depot before the depot\u2019s latest allowable return time. Each vehicle performs one outbound trip that visits a sequence of customers and then returns to the depot.\n\nChallenge\nWe need to determine which customers each vehicle will serve, in what order, and the resulting schedules so that every customer is visited exactly once, service starts within each customer\u2019s stated time window, and all vehicles return to the depot before it closes for the day. Travel time between any two locations is assumed to be the straight-line distance between their coordinates with an implicit speed of 1, so distance units equal time units.\n\nKey Requirements and Rules\n- Fleet and dispatch:\n  - Vehicles are identical and each is limited to a single trip.\n  - All vehicles depart the depot at time 0.\n  - A vehicle used on any route incurs a fixed deployment cost in addition to distance-based travel costs.\n  - The number of vehicles available for deployment is limited.\n- Coverage:\n  - Each customer must be visited exactly once; no split deliveries.\n- Time windows and waiting:\n  - Each customer has a delivery time window (earliest start and latest start).\n  - Service must begin within the customer\u2019s time window.\n  - If a vehicle arrives before the window opens, it must wait on site until the window opens.\n- Service times:\n  - Each customer requires a specified unloading/service time.\n  - The vehicle\u2019s departure from a customer occurs at (arrival time) + (service time), or (window open time) + (service time) if waiting occurred.\n- Capacity:\n  - Each vehicle has a maximum carrying capacity.\n  - The total demand served on any vehicle\u2019s route must not exceed that capacity at any point.\n- Depot return:\n  - All routes must end at the depot and the vehicle must arrive back before the depot\u2019s closing time.\n\nCost Considerations\n- Total cost combines the sum of travel distances across all routes and the fixed deployment cost for each vehicle used.\n- Unused vehicles do not incur deployment costs, so there is a trade-off between route consolidation (fewer vehicles, potentially longer routes and tighter schedules) and time-window feasibility (which may require additional vehicles to avoid late arrivals).\n\nGoal\nDevelop a set of routes and schedules that:\n- Visit every customer exactly once,\n- Begin service within each customer\u2019s time window (with waiting allowed if early),\n- Respect vehicle capacity and service time requirements,\n- Start from the depot at time 0 and return before the depot\u2019s closing time,\n- Minimize total travel distance plus the fixed cost of each vehicle deployed.\n\nANNEX \u2013 Operations Data\n- Depot location (coordinates): (50, 50)\n- Depot latest return time (closing): 293\n- Customer locations (coordinates): Customer Locations (coordinates):\n  - C1: (41, 83)\n  - C2: (20, 56)\n  - C3: (48, 35)\n  - C4: (86, 18)\n  - C5: (33, 9)\n- Customer demands (units): Customer Demands:\n  - C1: 11 units\n  - C2: 22 units\n  - C3: 19 units\n  - C4: 23 units\n  - C5: 24 units\n- Customer time windows (earliest start, latest start): Customer Time Windows [earliest, latest]:\n  - C1: [53, 123]\n  - C2: [31, 131]\n  - C3: [13, 106]\n  - C4: [48, 99]\n  - C5: [51, 125]\n- Customer service times: Service Times (minutes at customer):\n  - C1: 8\n  - C2: 14\n  - C3: 14\n  - C4: 13\n  - C5: 13\n- Vehicle capacity (units): 49\n- Number of vehicles available: 3\n- Fixed deployment cost per vehicle: 100.0",
    "LLM_description_template": "Subject: Routing and Scheduling Plan for Today\u2019s Multi-Stop Deliveries\n\nContext\nOur delivery operation dispatches a fleet of identical vehicles from a single central depot to serve a set of customer locations within the planning horizon. All vehicles begin their routes at time 0 and must be back at the depot before the depot\u2019s latest allowable return time. Each vehicle performs one outbound trip that visits a sequence of customers and then returns to the depot.\n\nChallenge\nWe need to determine which customers each vehicle will serve, in what order, and the resulting schedules so that every customer is visited exactly once, service starts within each customer\u2019s stated time window, and all vehicles return to the depot before it closes for the day. Travel time between any two locations is assumed to be the straight-line distance between their coordinates with an implicit speed of 1, so distance units equal time units.\n\nKey Requirements and Rules\n- Fleet and dispatch:\n  - Vehicles are identical and each is limited to a single trip.\n  - All vehicles depart the depot at time 0.\n  - A vehicle used on any route incurs a fixed deployment cost in addition to distance-based travel costs.\n  - The number of vehicles available for deployment is limited.\n- Coverage:\n  - Each customer must be visited exactly once; no split deliveries.\n- Time windows and waiting:\n  - Each customer has a delivery time window (earliest start and latest start).\n  - Service must begin within the customer\u2019s time window.\n  - If a vehicle arrives before the window opens, it must wait on site until the window opens.\n- Service times:\n  - Each customer requires a specified unloading/service time.\n  - The vehicle\u2019s departure from a customer occurs at (arrival time) + (service time), or (window open time) + (service time) if waiting occurred.\n- Capacity:\n  - Each vehicle has a maximum carrying capacity.\n  - The total demand served on any vehicle\u2019s route must not exceed that capacity at any point.\n- Depot return:\n  - All routes must end at the depot and the vehicle must arrive back before the depot\u2019s closing time.\n\nCost Considerations\n- Total cost combines the sum of travel distances across all routes and the fixed deployment cost for each vehicle used.\n- Unused vehicles do not incur deployment costs, so there is a trade-off between route consolidation (fewer vehicles, potentially longer routes and tighter schedules) and time-window feasibility (which may require additional vehicles to avoid late arrivals).\n\nGoal\nDevelop a set of routes and schedules that:\n- Visit every customer exactly once,\n- Begin service within each customer\u2019s time window (with waiting allowed if early),\n- Respect vehicle capacity and service time requirements,\n- Start from the depot at time 0 and return before the depot\u2019s closing time,\n- Minimize total travel distance plus the fixed cost of each vehicle deployed.\n\nANNEX \u2013 Operations Data\n- Depot location (coordinates): {DEPOT_LOCATION}\n- Depot latest return time (closing): {DEPOT_CLOSING_TIME}\n- Customer locations (coordinates): {CUSTOMER_LOCATIONS}\n- Customer demands (units): {CUSTOMER_DEMANDS}\n- Customer time windows (earliest start, latest start): {TIME_WINDOWS}\n- Customer service times: {SERVICE_TIMES}\n- Vehicle capacity (units): {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}\n- Number of vehicles available: {NUM_VEHICLES}\n- Fixed deployment cost per vehicle: {VEHICLE_FIXED_COST}"
